:: Start [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<div class="stamp">Case file 001</div>
<p class="meta">FBI Seattle Field Office · Thursday, November 25, 1971</p>
<h1>Flight 305</h1>
<p>It's Thanksgiving morning, and nobody in the Seattle office has slept. Your supervisor drops a folder on your desk.</p>
<p class="quote">"Last night a man hijacked Northwest Orient Flight 305, collected $200,000, and jumped out the back of the plane somewhere over the woods. We need two things by tonight: what happened, in order, and where to send the search teams. Seven leads. Go."</p>
<div class="how">
<p><b>How to investigate</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Visiting a new place uses one lead. Going back is free.</li>
<li>Interviews: two questions each. Witnesses won't always agree.</li>
<li>Cards marked <b>One witness</b> rest on a single person's memory. Two witnesses agreeing is stronger.</li>
<li>Newspaper rumors aren't evidence. Keep them off your timeline.</li>
<li>Build the night in order on the <b>timeline board</b>. Connect clues on the <b>deduction board</b>. Both are free.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="actions">[[Start investigating|Hub]]</div>


:: Hub
<<if $leads lte 0>><<goto "OutOfLeads">><</if>>
<<set _ev to setup.events.filter(function(e){ return $leads <= e.at && !$events.includes(e.id); })>>
<<for _e range _ev>><<run $events.push(_e.id)>>
<<if _e.kind is "headline">><div class="headline"><span class="paper">Seattle Post-Intelligencer</span><<print _e.text>></div>
<<else>><p class="quote chief"><<print _e.text>></p><</if>>
<</for>>
<h2>Where to?</h2>
<p class="meta">New places cost a lead. Places you've visited are free to revisit.</p>
<<casemap>>
<details class="maplist"><summary>Show the places as a list</summary>
<ul class="map">
<li><<maplink "Gate" "🎫 Portland airport: the ticket counter and gate">></li>
<li><<maplink "Schaffner" "🗣️ Interview flight attendant Florence Schaffner">></li>
<li><<maplink "Mucklow" "🗣️ Interview flight attendant Tina Mucklow">></li>
<li><<maplink "Cockpit" "👨‍✈️ Interview the cockpit crew">></li>
<li><<maplink "Mitchell" "💺 Interview passenger Bill Mitchell">></li>
<li><<maplink "Plane" "✈️ Search the plane in Reno">></li>
<li><<maplink "MoneyRoom" "💵 The FBI money room">></li>
<li><<maplink "Escort" "🛩️ McChord Air Force Base: the chase pilots">></li>
<li><<maplink "Newsroom" "📰 A newspaper office">></li>
</ul>
</details>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Timeline board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Timeline">><</link>><<link "Deduction board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[I'm ready to report|Report]]</div>


:: OutOfLeads
<h2>Out of leads</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"That's all the time we have," your supervisor says. "Let's hear your report."</p>
<div class="actions"><<link "One last look at the timeline">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Timeline">><</link>><<link "One last look at the deduction board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[Make your report|Report]]</div>


:: Timeline
<h2>Timeline board</h2>
<p class="meta">Tap the events in the order they happened. You can only place events you have a clue for. Tap "Clear" to start over.</p>
<div id="tlboard"><<include "TimelineCards">></div>
<div class="actions"><<link "Back">><<goto $return>><</link>></div>


:: TimelineCards
<<set _have to setup.timeline.filter(function(t){ return $notebook.includes(t.need); })>>
<<set _left to _have.filter(function(t){ return !$tl.includes(t.id); }).sort(function(a,b){ return a.text.localeCompare(b.text); })>>
<h3>Your timeline</h3>
<<if $tl.length is 0>><p class="slot-empty">Nothing placed yet.</p>
<<else>><ol class="timeline"><<for _id range $tl>><li><<print setup.timeline.find(function(t){ return t.id === _id; }).text>></li><</for>></ol><</if>>
<<if _have.length is 0>><p class="note">You don't have any timeline clues yet. Interviews and the plane are good places to start.</p>
<<elseif _left.length gt 0>>
<h3>Place next</h3>
<div class="choices">
<<for _t range _left>><<capture _t>><span class="opt"><<link _t.text>><<run $tl.push(_t.id)>><<replace "#tlboard">><<include "TimelineCards">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>>
</div>
<<else>><p class="note">All the events you have clues for are placed.</p><</if>>
<<if $tl.length gt 0>><div class="actions secondary"><<link "Clear">><<set $tl to []>><<replace "#tlboard">><<include "TimelineCards">><</replace>><</link>></div><</if>>
<p class="meta">Events found: <<print _have.length>> of <<print setup.timeline.length>></p>


:: Gate
<h2>Portland airport</h2>
<p>Portland International, the afternoon before Thanksgiving. Families with suitcases, a long line at the Northwest Orient counter. The gate agent, Hal Williams, checked in hundreds of people yesterday.</p>
<p class="quote">"A man paid cash for a one-way ticket to Seattle. Name on the ticket: Dan Cooper. Honestly, I barely remember him. He looked like every other businessman going home for the holiday."</p>
<<clue "ticket">>
<<clue "plain">>
<<tomap>>


:: Schaffner
<h2>Interview: Florence Schaffner</h2>
<p>Florence Schaffner sat in the jump seat at the back of the plane, right next to the man in the last row. She's tired but sharp.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "schaffner">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "schaffner">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Mucklow
<h2>Interview: Tina Mucklow</h2>
<p>Tina Mucklow spent more time near the hijacker than anyone: from Seattle until just before the jump. She stayed calm the whole night.</p>
<<clue "polite">>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "mucklow">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "mucklow">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Cockpit
<h2>Interview: the cockpit crew</h2>
<p>Captain William Scott, First Officer Bill Rataczak and Flight Engineer Harold Anderson spent the whole night locked in the cockpit, taking orders by phone from the back of the plane.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "cockpit">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "cockpit">></div>
<<clue "takeoff">>
<<tomap>>


:: Mitchell
<h2>Interview: passenger Bill Mitchell</h2>
<p>Bill Mitchell, a college student, sat across the aisle from the man in the last row. He had no idea a hijacking was happening until he got off in Seattle.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "mitchell">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "mitchell">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Plane
<h2>The plane in Reno</h2>
<<include "Scene">>
<p>The Boeing 727 sits on the runway in Reno, its back stairs still hanging down. Agents are dusting every surface for fingerprints.</p>
<<clue "gone">>
<<clue "chutes">>
<p>Left behind on and around his seat in the last row:</p>
<<clue "tie">>
<<clue "butts">>
<<clue "prints">>
<p class="note">Everything you collect is bagged for your evidence locker.</p>
<<tomap>>


:: MoneyRoom
<h2>The FBI money room</h2>
<p>Yesterday afternoon, agents and bank workers raced to collect $200,000 in $20 bills. An agent shows you rolls of microfilm.</p>
<p class="quote">"Before it went on the plane, we photographed every single bill. Ten thousand twenties. If even one turns up anywhere, we'll know it's his."</p>
<<clue "serials">>
<<clue "circle">>
<<tomap>>


:: Escort
<h2>McChord Air Force Base</h2>
<p>The chase pilots look exhausted. Two fighter jets and a slower training plane followed Flight 305 south, weaving back and forth behind it.</p>
<p class="quote">"Thick clouds, no moon, sleet. We could barely see the airliner, let alone a man jumping out the back."</p>
<<clue "escort">>
<<clue "weather">>
<<clue "route">>
<<tomap>>


:: Newsroom
<h2>The newspaper office</h2>
<p>Phones ring nonstop. Reporters shout across desks. Everyone wants to know who the hijacker was.</p>
<p class="quote">"Only an army paratrooper would jump like that," one reporter says. "Bet he had a car waiting in the woods," says another.</p>
<<clue "pro">>
<<clue "escaped">>
<<clue "seattlejump">>
<<clue "name">>
<<tomap>>


:: Report [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Report</div>
<h2>Your report</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"Three things," your supervisor says. "What happened in order, what he looks like, and where we search."</p>

<h3>1. The timeline</h3>
<<if $tl.length is 0>><p class="note">You haven't built a timeline. You can still go back to the board.</p><<else>><ol class="timeline"><<for _id range $tl>><li><<print setup.timeline.find(function(t){ return t.id === _id; }).text>></li><</for>></ol><</if>>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Edit the timeline">><<set $return to "Report">><<goto "Timeline">><</link>></div>

<h3>2. Build the wanted poster</h3>
<p class="meta">Pick one line for each part of the description.</p>
<div id="descs"><<include "DescList">></div>

<h3>3. Where should the searchers go?</h3>
<div id="zones"><<include "ZoneList">></div>

<div id="file"><<include "ReportButton">></div>


:: DescList
<<set _parts to [
  ["ph", "Height and build", [["att","About 5 ft 10 to 6 ft (both flight attendants)"],["mitch","About 5 ft 9 and slim (Bill Mitchell)"],["range","5 ft 9 to 6 ft: witnesses differ"]]],
  ["pa", "Age", [["mid","Mid-forties (both flight attendants)"],["young","Late twenties: only a young daredevil would jump"]]],
  ["pe", "Hair and eyes", [["brown","Dark hair, brown eyes (both flight attendants)"],["skip","Leave hair and eyes off the poster"]]]
]>>
<div class="poster"><p class="poster-head">WANTED · FBI</p>
<<for _p range _parts>><<capture _p>><p class="poster-part"><<print _p[1]>></p>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _p[2]>><<capture _o>><span @class="State.variables[_p[0]] === _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<run State.variables[_p[0]] = _o[0]>><<set $desc to $ph + "," + $pa + "," + $pe>><<replace "#descs">><<include "DescList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "ReportButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>
<</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ZoneList
<<set _opts to [["ariel","North of the Lewis River, near Ariel and Lake Merwin"],["south","Farther south, toward Portland's northern suburbs"],["seattle","Around Seattle, where he got the money"],["reno","Near Reno, where the plane landed"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$zone is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $zone to _o[0]>><<replace "#zones">><<include "ZoneList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "ReportButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ReportButton
<<if $ph is "" or $pa is "" or $pe is "" or $zone is "">><p class="note">Finish the wanted poster and choose a search area to file your report.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[File my report|Verdict]]</div><</if>>


:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _order to setup.timeline.filter(function(t){ return !t.fake; }).map(function(t){ return t.id; })>>
<<set _hasFake to $tl.some(function(id){ return _order.indexOf(id) < 0; })>>
<<set _inOrder to $tl.every(function(id, i){ return i === 0 || _order.indexOf(id) > _order.indexOf($tl[i-1]); })>>
<<set $tlOk to _inOrder and not _hasFake and $tl.length gte 6>>
<<set _s1 to $tlOk>>
<<set _twoAgree to $notebook.includes("descS") and $notebook.includes("descM")>>
<<set _posterOk to ($ph is "att" or $ph is "range") and $pa is "mid" and $pe is "brown">>
<<set _s2 to _posterOk and _twoAgree>>
<<set _hasWindow to $notebook.includes("d_window") or ($notebook.includes("bump") and ($notebook.includes("route") or $notebook.includes("estimates")))>>
<<set _goodZone to $zone is "ariel" or $zone is "south">>
<<set _s3 to _goodZone and _hasWindow>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<if $stars is 3>><div class="stamp solved">Report accepted</div><<else>><div class="stamp">Report filed</div><</if>>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 3 stars</h2>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>The night, in order.</b> <<if _s1>>Your timeline has <<print $tl.length>> events, all in the right order.<<elseif _hasFake>>Your timeline includes a rumor that no evidence backs up. Rumors don't go on the timeline.<<elseif $tl.length lt 6>>Your timeline has only <<print $tl.length>> events. Searchers need more of the night pieced together.<<else>>Some events are out of order. Check when the passengers got off compared with the circling.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>A fair wanted poster.</b> <<if _s2>><<if $ph is "range">>You used what two witnesses agree on, and were honest that the height is uncertain. Real detectives do exactly this.<<else>>Every line on your poster is backed by two witnesses who agree.<</if>><<elseif not _twoAgree>>You never heard from both flight attendants, so you can't know their descriptions agree.<<elseif $pa is "young">>Nobody who saw him said "late twenties." That came from a newspaper guess.<<elseif $ph is "mitch">>You trusted one witness's height over two who agree.<<else>>Two witnesses agree on his dark hair and brown eyes. That's worth putting on the poster.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>A search area backed by evidence.</b> <<if _s3>>You used the bump time and the route to pick a spot along the flight path.<<elseif _goodZone>>That spot is on the flight path, but you didn't collect the clues that prove it: the bump time and where the plane was.<<else>>He couldn't have jumped there. The bump came long after Seattle and long before Reno.<</if>></li>
</ul>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><div @class="'card ' + setup.cards[_id].type"><span class="tag"><<print setup.typeLabel[setup.cards[_id].type]>></span><span class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></span></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[What really happened|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What really happened</h2>
<p>The real FBI pieced together the same night you did. Their first computer estimate sent searchers to the thick forest near Ariel and Lake Merwin, north of the Lewis River. Soldiers, police and volunteers searched for weeks and found nothing. Later, people working on the case (including the co-pilot) argued the jump happened farther south.</p>
<p>Witnesses really did disagree about his height and build, so his wanted poster was a best guess. And his name was never D.B. A reporter's mistake gave him that nickname.</p>
<p>He was never identified. But nine years later, a surprise turned up on a riverbank. That's your next case.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>Put events in order before you decide anything.</li>
<li>Two witnesses who agree beat one who doesn't.</li>
<li>Small facts, like the exact minute of a bump, can point a whole search.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">Interview answers are written for this game, based on what the real witnesses told the FBI.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<<run setup.lockerSave("001", $notebook)>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 001, Part 1 complete</h2>
<p>Your evidence has been bagged for Part 2.</p>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 3</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<p>Tell Rocky where you sent the searchers and which clues told you to.</p>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>


